  "caption": "3:07am: Quinn was fast asleep until a calf turned to rock and the hopping began.\n\nNight calf cramps are very common, become more frequent with age, and are usually harmless, even if they feel dramatic.\n\nWhat can help: a gentle wall calf stretch before bed, building calf strength with slow calf raises, loosening tight bedding that keeps your toes pointed, drinking enough water and pacing big days. When a cramp hits, pull your toes towards you and stretch it firmly, then walk it out. Bananas alone aren't a reliable shield.\n\nGet checked if cramps are frequent or worsening, or come with weakness or numbness. A calf that is swollen or red on one side needs a same-day medical check.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
